    "id": 897016,
    "name": "Shiro plums",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Shiro plums are large, round, yellow plums with a mild, sweet flavor and a slightly tart skin. Their flesh is juicy, translucent, and has a tender, melting texture. Shiro plums are great for fresh eating, cooking, canning, and dessert. Some say that Shiro plum jam has a flavor similar to pear butter, with notes of candied lemon and soft floral sweetness.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Shiro plum is a popular, heirloom Japanese plum introduced in 1899 by Luther Burbank.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Famous for its translucent, golden-yellow skin and incredibly sweet, juicy flesh.&nbsp; It is prized for fresh eating, baking, and canning.&nbsp;I also dry them for a sweet/tart treat in my mixed dried fruit bags.</span></p>",
